        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think this won't be a part of 'mini.tabline'. Mostly for two reasons:\r\n- It will indeed lead to almost complete refactor of existing code plus adding new one (with documentation close to the size of existing one). Not a huge deal considering current size, but still.\r\n- I kind of like that it is intended to work with `:bnext`/`:bprev`. Once the door of custom order is opened, it would lead to other complications. Like the new 'mini.bracketed' has `[b` and `]b` for navigating through buffers which uses natural buffer order right now. If this feature is implemented, those would need to account for it.\r\n\r\nThat said, I'd like to recommend looking at new ['mini.bracketed'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-bracketed.md). Besides `[b`/`]b` for buffers, it also has `[o`/`]o` for recently used files. I noticed that it completely removed my need for visually pairing related buffers for easier switching between 2 and more buffers.\r\n\r\nAll in all, unfortunately I'll close this. Thanks for suggestion, though!",
